# Intentfile (A2ML Canonical) — Enaction Engine north-star contractile

@abstract:
Enaction Engine is a deterministic, type-safe game engine for worlds shaped
through perception, affect, intention, action and consequence. Its current
implemented surface is the enaction-time deterministic timing substrate.
@end

## Purpose

Grow complete game-engine facilities through real proving-ground use, working
implementation, tests, and host-neutral boundaries. Cognition, affect, and
conation are sibling dimensions. Games retain their domain ontology.

## Anti-Purpose

Do not claim unimplemented engine facilities, create empty subsystem crates,
feed render interpolation into simulation, couple the runtime to UMS Studio, or
encode one game's ontology into low-level deterministic facilities.

[[intents]]

### preserve-deterministic-substrate
- description: Keep whole-step simulation and render-only interpolation enforced
- verification: cargo test --workspace
- status: active

### prove-through-games
- description: Validate reusable boundaries first through IDApTIK and then against Chronicles of Slavia
- verification: review integration evidence and provenance before extraction
- status: active

### maintain-canonical-identity
- description: Keep repository, crate, package, URL, container, and machine-readable identities aligned
- verification: repository-wide legacy-identity search and RSR verification
- status: active

[[wishes]]

### near
- description: Exercise enaction-time through a real game-host contract

### mid
- description: Establish a deterministic world-state and event substrate

### far
